# Lothar Cleanup

Invoked when the user asks to clean up / reset and [lothar.mdc](lothar.mdc) tells you to read and follow this file (`alwaysApply: false`). Reset the **current workspace root** to accelerator-only so they can bootstrap again in the same Cursor window. **You** run all steps via the terminal and file writes. Never tell the user to delete files themselves.

## Confirm first (required — do not run Execute until they agree)

On the **first** cleanup request in this thread, **stop** after asking for confirmation. Do **not** run terminal commands or delete files yet.

Reply with **one short sentence** explaining the action, then ask them to confirm. Use this wording (adapt only if the repo clearly has no storefront yet):

> I'll remove the bootstrapped storefront from this workspace and keep only `.cursor/` and `lothar-docs/` so you can bootstrap again — uncommitted store files will be deleted.

Then ask explicitly, e.g. **“Proceed with cleanup?”** or **“Yes to reset?”**

Proceed to **Execute** only after they clearly agree (e.g. “yes”, “proceed”, “confirm”). If they decline or are vague, do not clean up.

If they already confirmed in the same message as the request (e.g. “yes, clean up”), you may run **Execute** immediately.

## Execute (you run this)

`REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)"`

**Never delete:** `.cursor/`, `lothar-docs/`, `.git/`

Remove all other top-level entries (storefront, `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env.local`, `accelerator.manifest.json`, root `README.md`, etc.):

```bash
REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)"
cd "$REPO_ROOT" || exit 1
for item in * .[!.]* ..?*; do
  [ -e "$item" ] || continue
  case "$item" in
    .cursor|lothar-docs|.git) ;;
    *) rm -rf "$item" ;;
  esac
done
```

**Restore** `$REPO_ROOT/.gitignore` to the accelerator default (overwrite):

```
# Lothar bootstrap
.lothar-clone-tmp

# Next.js / storefront (after bootstrap)
node_modules
dist
.next
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
*.log
```

Do **not** ignore `.cursor` in `.gitignore`.

## After success

Tell the user:

- Workspace reset — only `.cursor/`, `lothar-docs/`, and `.gitignore` remain at the repo root (plus `.git` history unchanged)
- They can bootstrap again here (e.g. “bootstrap B2C + Next”)
- If port 3000 is busy, stop any old `pnpm dev` process first

## Do not

- Run cleanup without user confirmation
- Delete `.git/` or run `git reset --hard` unless they explicitly ask to revert commits
- Remove `.cursor/` or `lothar-docs/`

